From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Graham <matt.sg@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:25:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] kernel: physical-address model, dispatch lock, bridge
 and file fixes

Runtime physical IDs with an exact contiguous-allocation table and a reserve
allocator above RAM replace the page allocator; reservations stay owned
through decommit. Without RECOMP_DISPATCH_GATE an always-on dispatch lock
serialises DISPATCH_LEVEL. The segment walker is the default pushbuffer
walk, RECOMP_PB_WALK=dma selects the DMA walk. File opens keep a
thread-local host error, read-only sharing and the deferred FATX overwrite;
a failed open reports a host error only when a host open was tried.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
